{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "10-system-design-50-workflows-20-run-50-process-lifecycle",
  "title": "Process Lifecycle",
  "root": "b-50-process-lifecycle-root",
  "blocks": {
    "b-50-process-lifecycle-root": {
      "id": "b-50-process-lifecycle-root",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "children": [
        "b-50-process-lifecycle-direct-spawn",
        "process-stable-name",
        "b-50-process-lifecycle-observation-heading",
        "b-50-process-lifecycle-observation",
        "b-50-process-lifecycle-settlement-heading",
        "b-50-process-lifecycle-settlement",
        "b-50-process-lifecycle-operator-heading",
        "b-50-process-lifecycle-operator"
      ]
    },
    "b-50-process-lifecycle-direct-spawn": {
      "id": "b-50-process-lifecycle-direct-spawn",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The managed-process controller starts "
        },
        {
          "insert": "run-loop",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " directly for a run that holds the dispatch lease. The command carries the required "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--lease-id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", so process execution remains bound to the authority acquired for that run without an intermediate supervisor."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "process-stable-name": {
      "id": "process-stable-name",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The dashboard-managed Melee process is named melee-live. Its saved process record and log paths keep that name across dashboard restarts. The detached run process can continue after the UI server exits, so process status and stop controls use the saved identity."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-process-lifecycle-observation-heading": {
      "id": "b-50-process-lifecycle-observation-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Observation and Signals"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-process-lifecycle-observation": {
      "id": "b-50-process-lifecycle-observation",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The controller tees the process streams into append-only files at "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<stateDir>/ui-processes/<name>.stdout.log",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<stateDir>/ui-processes/<name>.stderr.log",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Process status exposes both paths. On "
        },
        {
          "insert": "SIGINT",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "SIGTERM",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", the run loop requests a graceful stop and reaches its normal exit path."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-process-lifecycle-settlement-heading": {
      "id": "b-50-process-lifecycle-settlement-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Exit Settlement"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-process-lifecycle-settlement": {
      "id": "b-50-process-lifecycle-settlement",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The run loop's top-level finally calls settleRunOnExit. Normal settlement parks the run through settleStoppedRun and releases dispatch authority. If a sync successor acquires active authority, the exit handler advances its runtime. Unexpected database-closed or error exits use hardStopRun for emergency settlement. Normal settlement events retain guardian as a compatibility actor name."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-process-lifecycle-operator-heading": {
      "id": "b-50-process-lifecycle-operator-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Operator Recovery"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-process-lifecycle-operator": {
      "id": "b-50-process-lifecycle-operator",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The operator watches process status and the exposed stream logs. The controller does not restart a failed process or create incident files. A crash or SIGKILL can bypass normal exit settlement. Run the manual recover-claims job before resuming after such an exit."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
